{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791429644,"nonce":"LtMmv/8pRAV3NYEC5myL91jC8Bs=","title":"Cranelift: mark OSR request and transfer paths cold","message":"The native backend synthesizes threshold request branches and helper-transfer branches without telling Cranelift that these blocks are rare. The returning request call is reached once at the threshold, yet its ordinary frequency can influence register allocation in a hot vector loop. HIR cold-helper annotations do not cover these backend-generated blocks.\n\nUse Cranelift cold block metadata for entry/backedge promotion requests and one-way frame-transfer dispatch. Preserve all probes, thresholds, interpreter-first dispatch and transfer semantics. Validate the generated CLIF, real running-frame transfers, and same-executable short/long benchmark controls. This is independent of the held general final-tier probe removal, whose LU regression must not ship.","files":null}]}